# App Frontend Rules (uni-app x)

## Project Identity

- Framework: uni-app x (uni-app 2.0) + Vue 3 Composition API + TypeScript + Vite
- Platforms: H5 (primary), WeChat Mini Program (primary), iOS, Android, HarmonyOS
- IDE: HBuilderX ^3.99
- Runtime HTTP: `uni.request` only (no axios)

## File Organization

- Pages: `pages/<domain>/` with `.uvue` files (not `.vue`)
- Components: `components/` split by `business/` and `common/`
- API: `api/<domain>.ts` mirroring backend services (auth, user, child, assignment, content, voice)
- State: `stores/<domain>.ts` using Pinia Composition API style
- Utils: `utils/` for shared helpers; `styles/` for shared styles
- Static assets: `static/` (images, fonts)
- Platform-specific: `wxcomponents/` (WeChat), `nativeResources/` (App), `harmony-configs/` (HarmonyOS)

## Architecture Rules

- All HTTP calls go through `api/http.ts`. Never call `uni.request` directly outside it.
- API modules must match backend service boundaries. Do not create ad-hoc fetch in pages.
- Use Pinia stores for shared state; avoid passing deep props for cross-page data.
- Prefer Composition API with `<script setup>`.
- Never import backend proto types directly; use the TypeScript interfaces in `api/*.ts`.

## Naming Conventions

| Item | Style |
|---|---|
| File / folder | kebab-case |
| Vue component (file) | PascalCase |
| TS variable / function | camelCase |
| Pinia store | camelCase file, export `useXxxStore` |
| API function | camelCase, action-verb first (`sendSmsCode`, `fetchAssignments`) |
| Type / Interface | PascalCase |
| Constant | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE |

## Style

- Indent: 2 spaces
- Quotes: single (double when string contains single quotes)
- Semicolons: yes
- Max line length: 120 (soft)
- No trailing spaces

## Platform-Specific Constraints

### WeChat Mini Program
- `manifest.json` → `mp-weixin.urlCheck: false` for local dev
- All backend domains must be whitelisted in WeChat MP Console
- TLS 1.2+ required

### H5
- Standard CORS applies
- `Content-Type: application/json` auto-added in H5 path of `api/http.ts`

## Error Handling

- Business errors: backend returns `{ code, message, data }`. `code === 0` is success.
- `401` in `api/http.ts` triggers auto-logout and redirect to login page.
- Network errors: show `uni.showToast` with user-friendly messages; log detailed error to console.

## Testing

- Jest for unit tests
- Mock `uni.request` in tests
- Keep page tests in `pages/pages.test.js`

## Commit Style

- Follow the repo-wide Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`
- Scopes for this project: `app`, `pages`, `api`, `stores`, `components`, `utils`, `styles`, `manifest`, `tests`
- Subject in English or Chinese (consistent within this sub-repo)

## Forbidden

- Do not use axios or fetch directly
- Do not call backend `agent/` service directly; route through Go backend
- Do not hardcode backend URLs outside env variables
- Do not add new top-level directories without updating this rules file
- Do not use Options API for new components
